<main>

  <section id="abstract">
    <h2>Abstract</h2>
    <p>The purpose of this study is to examine the sustainability of Artificial Intelligence (AI) adoption in retail and e-commerce, particularly among TikTok Shop sellers in Malaysia. The rapid development of AI technology has encouraged businesses to use AI to improve their operations, customer experience, and business performance. This study focuses on examining the relationship between AI Adoption (IV1), Factors Influencing AI Adoption (IV2), Customer Satisfaction and Trust (IV3), and Environmental Sustainability (DV).</p>
    <p>This study uses a quantitative research approach, where data are collected through a structured questionnaire using a five-point Likert scale. The collected data are analysed using Partial Least Squares Structural Equation Modelling (PLS-SEM) through SmartPLS to examine the relationship between variables.</p>
    <p>The findings show that Customer Satisfaction and Trust (IV3) have the strongest positive relationship with Environmental Sustainability (DV), followed by Factors Influencing AI Adoption (IV2). However, AI Adoption (IV1) does not show a significant relationship with Environmental Sustainability (DV). The findings of this study provide a better understanding of how AI-related factors, as well as customer satisfaction and trust, may contribute to environmental sustainability among TikTok Shop sellers in Malaysia.</p>
    <p style="font-size:13px;"><strong>Keywords:</strong> Artificial Intelligence, AI Adoption, TikTok Shop Sellers, Customer Satisfaction and Trust, Environmental Sustainability, Retail and E-commerce, SmartPLS.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="introduction">
    <h2>Introduction</h2>
    <p>E-commerce in Malaysia grew quickly after the COVID-19 pandemic, and platforms such as TikTok Shop have become a major part of how Malaysians buy and sell products, commonly known as the "Yellow Basket" or "Beg Kuning." As competition among sellers increases, many TikTok Shop sellers are turning to Artificial Intelligence (AI) to improve their operations, attract customers, and increase sales. This study examines whether AI adoption, the factors that influence it, and customer satisfaction and trust actually contribute to environmental sustainability among these sellers.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="problem-statement">
    <h2>Problem Statement</h2>
    <p>TikTok Shop sellers face growing pressure to stay competitive, and many are turning to AI to help. However, it is still unclear whether AI adoption actually supports business sustainability, especially environmentally. Some sellers also face barriers to adopting AI, such as limited resources, skills, or external support. This study investigates how AI adoption affects environmental sustainability among TikTok Shop sellers in Malaysia.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="objectives">
    <h2>Research Objectives</h2>
    <div class="grid-2">
      <div class="card"><span class="tag">RO1</span><p>To evaluate the influence of organizational and external factors on AI adoption among TikTok Shop sellers in Malaysia.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><span class="tag">RO2</span><p>To evaluate the direct impact of AI adoption on customer sustainability among TikTok Shop sellers in Malaysia.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><span class="tag">RO3</span><p>To evaluate the direct impact of AI adoption on environmental sustainability among TikTok Shop sellers in Malaysia.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><span class="tag">RO4</span><p>To determine the overall combined effect of AI adoption on long-term business sustainability among TikTok Shop sellers in Malaysia.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="questions">
    <h2>Research Questions</h2>
    <div class="grid-2">
      <div class="card"><span class="tag">RQ1</span><p>How do organizational and external factors influence AI adoption among TikTok Shop sellers in Malaysia?</p></div>
      <div class="card"><span class="tag">RQ2</span><p>What is the direct effect of AI adoption on customer sustainability among TikTok Shop sellers in Malaysia?</p></div>
      <div class="card"><span class="tag">RQ3</span><p>What is the direct effect of AI adoption on environmental sustainability among TikTok Shop sellers in Malaysia?</p></div>
      <div class="card"><span class="tag">RQ4</span><p>How significantly does AI adoption contribute to overall long-term business sustainability among TikTok Shop sellers in Malaysia?</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="hypothesis">
    <h2>Hypothesis</h2>
    <div class="grid-2">
      <div class="card"><span class="tag">H1</span><p><strong>Demographic Profile &rarr; Environmental Sustainability.</strong> There is a significant difference in environmental sustainability among TikTok Shop sellers based on their demographic profiles. Prior TOE-based studies on Malaysian MSMEs have tested whether firm-level or individual characteristics moderate the strength of technology-adoption relationships, so gender, age, business type and years of experience are expected to shape how strongly AI-related factors translate into environmental outcomes.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><span class="tag">H2</span><p><strong>AI Adoption &rarr; Environmental Sustainability.</strong> There is a significant relationship between AI adoption and environmental sustainability. AI tools such as predictive inventory management are theorised to reduce overproduction and unsold stock, in line with how Diffusion of Innovation theory describes AI spreading through practical, observed benefits among peer sellers.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><span class="tag">H3</span><p><strong>Factors Influencing AI Adoption &rarr; Environmental Sustainability.</strong> There is a significant relationship between factors influencing AI adoption and environmental sustainability. The TOE framework explains that organizational conditions (management support, employee skills) and environmental conditions (cost, government support) determine whether AI is implemented effectively enough to support sustainable practices.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><span class="tag">H4</span><p><strong>Customer Satisfaction and Trust &rarr; Environmental Sustainability.</strong> There is a significant relationship between customer satisfaction and trust and environmental sustainability. Sellers who build stronger customer relationships through reliable AI interactions are more likely to sustain long-term operations, supporting continued investment in sustainable practices rather than short-term survival tactics.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="scope">
    <h2>Scope of Study</h2>
    <p>This study focuses on active TikTok Shop sellers operating in the retail and e-commerce industry in Malaysia. Data is collected through an online questionnaire distributed via WhatsApp and TikTok, examining sellers' experiences and perspectives on AI adoption and its role in business sustainability.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="significance">
    <h2>Significance of Study</h2>
    <p>This research adds to the limited literature on AI adoption among small and medium retail sellers, most existing studies focus on large corporations. Practically, it helps sellers plan their AI investment more wisely and helps government agencies design better support programs that also promote environmental sustainability.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="ethics">
    <h2>Ethical Considerations</h2>
    <p>This study was conducted in an ethical manner from the design stage through to the reporting of findings. Participation in the survey was voluntary, and respondents had the right to withdraw at any time without penalty. Before answering the questionnaire, respondents were informed of the purpose of the study and how their data would be used.</p>
    <p>All information collected from respondents was kept confidential and used only for academic purposes. No personal identifying information is disclosed in the findings, and data is reported in combined form to protect respondent identity. The researchers conducted this study in good faith and reported the findings honestly, even where results did not support the hypotheses. All sources used in this study are properly cited to avoid plagiarism.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="literature-review">
    <h2>Literature Review</h2>
    <h3>Underpinning Theory</h3>
    <p>This study is grounded in the <strong>Diffusion of Innovation (DOI) Theory</strong> linked to the <strong>Technology-Organization-Environment (TOE) Framework</strong>. DOI theory explains how AI tools such as chatbots and inventory systems spread among TikTok Shop sellers as they observe the results achieved by similar businesses. The TOE framework explains AI adoption through three factors: technology, organization (management support, employee skills), and environment (cost, government support).</p>

    <h3 style="margin-top:28px;">Variables of Study</h3>
    <div class="grid-2">
      <div class="card var-card"><span class="tag">IV1</span><h3>AI Adoption</h3><p>The extent to which a business incorporates AI tools such as chatbots, product recommendation systems, and inventory management software into daily operations. Measured as a matter of degree rather than a simple yes/no decision.</p></div>
      <div class="card var-card"><span class="tag">IV2</span><h3>Factors Influencing AI Adoption</h3><p>The organizational and environmental conditions that determine how readily a business adopts AI, including cost, management support, employee skills, and government support.</p></div>
      <div class="card var-card"><span class="tag">IV3</span><h3>Customer Satisfaction and Trust</h3><p>How positively customers evaluate their experience with a business's AI-enabled tools, and how much confidence they place in those tools when making purchasing decisions.</p></div>
      <div class="card var-card"><span class="tag">DV</span><h3>Environmental Sustainability</h3><p>A business's ability to reduce its negative impact on the environment, such as through reduced waste, more efficient resource use, and lower energy consumption, while remaining commercially viable.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="card var-card" style="margin-top:16px;"><span class="tag">MODERATOR</span><h3>Demographic Profile</h3><p>Background characteristics of sellers (gender, age, type of business, years of experience) expected to influence the strength of the relationships above, rather than affecting environmental sustainability directly.</p></div>
  </section>

  <section id="methodology">
    <h2>Research Methodology</h2>
    <h3>Research Design</h3>
    <p>A quantitative approach with a cross-sectional, cause-and-effect design. Data is collected once from TikTok Shop sellers to test how AI Adoption, Factors Influencing AI Adoption, and Customer Satisfaction and Trust directly influence Environmental Sustainability, while examining the moderating role of Demographic Profile.</p>

    <h3 style="margin-top:20px;">Population &amp; Sampling</h3>
    <p>Active TikTok Shop sellers operating in Malaysia. Since no centralized sampling frame exists, this study uses convenience sampling, targeting sellers who currently use or have previously used AI tools. A minimum sample of 100 respondents will be collected, sufficient to support PLS-SEM analysis.</p>

    <h3 style="margin-top:20px;">Measurement &amp; Scaling</h3>
    <p>A five-point Likert scale (1 = Strongly Disagree, 5 = Strongly Agree) across four constructs, each measured with five items. Demographic information is measured using nominal and ordinal categorical items.</p>

    <div class="item-block">
      <h4>AI Adoption (IV1)</h4>
      <div class="item-row"><div class="item-code">AI1</div><div class="item-text">AI adoption improves the sustainability of the retail/e-commerce business.</div></div>
      <div class="item-row"><div class="item-code">AI2</div><div class="item-text">AI helps the business operate more efficiently.</div></div>
      <div class="item-row"><div class="item-code">AI3</div><div class="item-text">AI adoption helps reduce the environmental impact of the business.</div></div>
      <div class="item-row"><div class="item-code">AI4</div><div class="item-text">AI supports sustainable business practices in the organization.</div></div>
      <div class="item-row"><div class="item-code">AI5</div><div class="item-text">The organization considers AI integration as a long-term strategic priority for business growth.</div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="item-block">
      <h4>Factors Influencing AI Adoption (IV2)</h4>
      <div class="item-row"><div class="item-code">FA1</div><div class="item-text">The benefits of AI encourage the organization to adopt AI.</div></div>
      <div class="item-row"><div class="item-code">FA2</div><div class="item-text">The cost of AI influences the organization's decision to adopt AI.</div></div>
      <div class="item-row"><div class="item-code">FA3</div><div class="item-text">Management support encourages AI adoption in the organization.</div></div>
      <div class="item-row"><div class="item-code">FA4</div><div class="item-text">Employee skills influence the organization's ability to adopt AI.</div></div>
      <div class="item-row"><div class="item-code">FA5</div><div class="item-text">Government initiatives and regulatory support encourage the organization to adopt AI.</div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="item-block">
      <h4>Customer Satisfaction and Trust (IV3)</h4>
      <div class="item-row"><div class="item-code">CS1</div><div class="item-text">AI-driven personalization like product recommendations and chatbots enhances overall customer satisfaction.</div></div>
      <div class="item-row"><div class="item-code">CS2</div><div class="item-text">Customers respond positively to the use of AI tools in the TikTok Shop operations.</div></div>
      <div class="item-row"><div class="item-code">CS3</div><div class="item-text">AI adoption improves customer trust and brand loyalty.</div></div>
      <div class="item-row"><div class="item-code">CS4</div><div class="item-text">AI tools help the business respond to customer needs faster.</div></div>
      <div class="item-row"><div class="item-code">CS5</div><div class="item-text">Customers are more likely to make repeat purchases when AI is used in the TikTok Shop.</div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="item-block">
      <h4>Environmental Sustainability (DV)</h4>
      <div class="item-row"><div class="item-code">ES1</div><div class="item-text">AI helps reduce energy consumption in the business.</div></div>
      <div class="item-row"><div class="item-code">ES2</div><div class="item-text">AI helps reduce waste in business operations.</div></div>
      <div class="item-row"><div class="item-code">ES3</div><div class="item-text">AI helps the business use resources more efficiently.</div></div>
      <div class="item-row"><div class="item-code">ES4</div><div class="item-text">AI adoption contributes to better environmental sustainability.</div></div>
      <div class="item-row"><div class="item-code">ES5</div><div class="item-text">The organization plans to increase AI usage to further support environmental sustainability goals.</div></div>
    </div>

    <h3 style="margin-top:20px;">Data Collection</h3>
    <p>The questionnaire is distributed online through direct messaging on TikTok, Threads, and WhatsApp, targeting sellers who currently use AI in their operations. A reminder is sent approximately one week after initial distribution.</p>

    <h3 style="margin-top:20px;">Data Analysis</h3>
    <p>Data is analyzed using SmartPLS (Partial Least Squares Structural Equation Modeling). Indicator reliability, path coefficients, and the R-square value are examined, followed by bootstrapping to test the significance of each hypothesized relationship.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="findings">
    <h2>Findings &amp; Results</h2>
    <p>Following model restructuring &mdash; where the weakest indicator (Y5) was removed from Environmental Sustainability to improve reliability &mdash; the final model produced the results below.</p>

    <h3 style="margin-top:20px;">Indicator Reliability</h3>
    <table class="results-table">
      <tr><th>Construct</th><th>Highest Indicators</th><th>Lowest Indicator</th></tr>
      <tr><td>AI Adoption (IV1)</td><td class="num">0.839 &ndash; 0.878</td><td class="num">0.592</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Factors Influencing AI Adoption (IV2)</td><td class="num">0.779 &ndash; 0.867</td><td class="num">0.613</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Customer Satisfaction and Trust (IV3)</td><td class="num">0.768 &ndash; 0.866</td><td class="num">0.689</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Environmental Sustainability (DV)</td><td class="num">0.814 &ndash; 0.922</td><td class="num">&mdash;</td></tr>
    </table>
    <p>All retained indicator values fall within the acceptable range and were kept in the model.</p>

    <h3 style="margin-top:20px;">Path Coefficients &amp; R&sup2;</h3>
    <table class="results-table">
      <tr><th>Relationship</th><th>Path Coefficient</th></tr>
      <tr><td>AI Adoption &rarr; Environmental Sustainability</td><td class="num">0.073</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Factors Influencing AI Adoption &rarr; Environmental Sustainability</td><td class="num">0.368</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Customer Satisfaction and Trust &rarr; Environmental Sustainability</td><td class="num">0.447</td></tr>
    </table>
    <p>The R&sup2; value for Environmental Sustainability is <strong>0.576 (57.6%)</strong>, meaning the three independent variables explain 57.6% of the variance in Environmental Sustainability &mdash; a moderate level of explanatory power. The remaining 42.4% is explained by factors outside this study.</p>

    <h3 style="margin-top:20px;">Hypothesis Testing (Bootstrapping)</h3>
    <table class="results-table">
      <tr><th>Hypothesis</th><th>Relationship</th><th>p-value</th><th>Result</th></tr>
      <tr><td>H2</td><td>AI Adoption &rarr; Environmental Sustainability</td><td class="num">0.725</td><td class="num"><span class="pill rejected">Not Supported</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>H3</td><td>Factors Influencing AI Adoption &rarr; Environmental Sustainability</td><td class="num">0.044</td><td class="num"><span class="pill supported">Supported</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>H4</td><td>Customer Satisfaction and Trust &rarr; Environmental Sustainability</td><td class="num">0.010</td><td class="num"><span class="pill supported">Supported</span></td></tr>
    </table>
    <p>Using the 0.05 significance threshold, Customer Satisfaction and Trust (p = 0.010) and Factors Influencing AI Adoption (p = 0.044) both show a significant relationship with Environmental Sustainability. AI Adoption alone (p = 0.725) does not meet the required significance level, meaning AI adoption on its own does not significantly predict environmental sustainability among TikTok Shop sellers &mdash; it is the surrounding organizational factors and customer trust that drive the effect.</p>
  </section>

